 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 532677,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Find the surface area and the volume of the octagonal figure shown.<br>\n<figure>\n<img src=\"exercises/media/b9552a23ef983189.png\" alt=\"An octagonal prism. One of the sides of the octagon is labeled w equals 3 centimeters. The apothem is labeled a equals 4 centimeters. The height of the prism is labeled h equals 10 centimeters.\">\n</figure>",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>The surface area of a right prism where <i>B</i> is the area of the base, <i>p</i> is the perimeter of the base, and <i>h</i> is the height is <span data-math=\"SA = 2B + ph\"></span>.</p>\n<p>The apothem of a regular polygon is a line segment that starts at the center and is perpendicular to a side. The area of a regular polygon with apothem <i>a</i> and perimeter <i>p</i> is <span data-math=\"A = \\frac{1}{2}ap\"></span>.</p>\n<p>A regular octagon has eight sides of equal length. Therefore, the perimeter is:</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"p = 8(3{\\text{ cm)  =  24 cm}}\"></span>.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"A = \\frac{1}{2}ap = \\frac{1}{2}\\left( {4{\\text{ cm}}} \\right)\\left( {{\\text{24 cm}}} \\right) = 48{\\text{ c}}{{\\text{m}}^2}\"></span>, which in the surface area formula is <i>B.</i></p>\n<p>The surface area <span data-math=\"= {\\text{ }}2B + ph = {\\text{ }}2\\left( {48{\\text{ c}}{{\\text{m}}^2}} \\right){\\text{ }} + {\\text{ }}\\left( {24{\\text{ cm}}} \\right)\\left( {10{\\text{ cm}}} \\right){\\text{ }} = {\\text{ }}96{\\text{ c}}{{\\text{m}}^2} + {\\text{ }}240{\\text{ c}}{{\\text{m}}^2} = {\\text{ }}336{\\text{ c}}{{\\text{m}}^2}\"></span>.</p>\n<p>The surface area is 336 square centimeters.</p>\n<p>The volume of a right prism is <span data-math=\"V = Bh\"></span> <span data-math=\"= {\\text{ }}\\left( {48{\\text{ c}}{{\\text{m}}^2}} \\right)\\left( {{\\text{ }}10{\\text{ cm}}} \\right){\\text{ }} = {\\text{ }}480{\\text{ c}}{{\\text{m}}^3}\"></span>.</p>\n<p>The volume is 480 cubic centimeters.</p>\n"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"\\begin{array}{rcl}\n{SA}&amp;{ = }&amp;{336\\text{ cm}{^2}}\\\\ \n{V}&amp;{ = }&amp;{480\\text{ cm}{^3}}\\\\ \\end{array}\">\\begin{array}{rcl}\n{SA}&amp;{ = }&amp;{336\\text{ cm}{^2}}\\\\ \n{V}&amp;{ = }&amp;{480\\text{ cm}{^3}}\\\\ \\end{array}\"</span>"
    }
   ],
